tools.example:
1. Build a selection and run Select > Save Selection..., name it "subject".
2. Later, Select > Load Selection..., Channel = subject, Operation = New Selection.
3. Select > Transform Selection, hold Alt+Shift and scale it down 5% from the centre, press Enter.

JSX:
var doc = app.activeDocument;
var ch = doc.channels.add(); ch.name = "subject";
doc.selection.store(ch);
doc.selection.load(ch, SelectionType.REPLACE);

1. Finish editing in 16-bit RGB.
2. Image > Duplicate to keep the master safe.
3. Image > Mode > 8 Bits/Channel, then Image > Mode > CMYK Color with the printer's profile set in Edit > Color Settings.

JSX: app.activeDocument.changeMode(ChangeMode.CMYK);
app.activeDocument.bitsPerChannel = BitsPerChannelType.EIGHT;

1. Alt+Ctrl+I.
2. Untick Resample, set Resolution to 300 ppi - the pixel count is unchanged and the print size shrinks.
3. To actually resize: tick Resample, Width 1600 px, Resample = Bicubic Sharper.

JSX:
app.preferences.rulerUnits = Units.PIXELS;
app.activeDocument.resizeImage(UnitValue(1600,'px'), null, 72, ResampleMethod.BICUBICSHARPER);

1. Image > Image Rotation > Arbitrary..., 1.8 degrees Clockwise, to level a scan.
2. Crop away the resulting transparent corners, or use the Crop tool's Content-Aware option to fill them.

JSX: app.activeDocument.rotateCanvas(90);

1. Hide the background layer so the icon sits on transparency.
2. Image > Trim..., Based On = Transparent Pixels, all four sides ticked.

JSX: app.activeDocument.trim(TrimType.TRANSPARENT, true, true, true, true);

JSX:
var work = app.activeDocument.duplicate("export", true);
work.flatten();
var o = new JPEGSaveOptions(); o.quality = 10;
work.saveAs(new File("C:/out/export.jpg"), o, true);
work.close(SaveOptions.DONOTSAVECHANGES);

Inside a batch loop:
for (var i = 0; i < files.length; i++) {
  var doc = app.open(files[i]);
  // ... work ...
  doc.close(SaveOptions.DONOTSAVECHANGES);
  app.purge(PurgeTarget.ALLCACHES);
}
